From: Carlos Cabrera H. <6750732+ccabrerah@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 28] ggml-sycl: 2-4-column wide Q8_0 matvec (GGML_SYCL_Q8W_NCOLS)

GGML_SYCL_Q8W_NCOLS=1 (with GGML_SYCL_Q8W=1). A speculative-decoding verify step multiplies the dense Q8_0 weights by
2-4 activation columns. Those went through the stock reorder ncols kernel (2-byte loads, two lanes per block), while
one column runs on patch 18's wide kernel (a whole block per lane in two 16-byte loads). This is the wide kernel for 2-4
columns: each lane loads a weight block once and dots it with every column's q8_1 block. Per column, the accumulation
and the sub-group reduction are the one-column kernel's, so column c's result equals that kernel's for column c alone.

--- a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/mmvq.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/mmvq.cpp
@@ -1257,6 +1257,72 @@
